# What is never part of a build context.
#
# The build context of a project image is the project root (specifications/
# core/PSS-project-settings-storage.md PSS-FR-26), and both backends send that
# whole tree to the Docker daemon before the first build step runs. Without
# this file the tree is dominated by compiler and package-manager output —
# `src-tauri/target` alone is tens of gigabytes on a developer machine — and the
# upload takes longer than the daemon's own answer is waited for, which is a
# build that fails on a timeout without one line of build output.
#
# Nothing named here is an input to any image this repository builds. No
# Dockerfile is excluded: the Docker Engine backend names the Dockerfile inside
# the context, so a Dockerfile left out of the context cannot be built.

# Rust build output, at every depth: src-tauri, server, and the mock CLI each
# carry one.
**/target

# Node package trees and frontend build output.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
dist
dist-ssr

# Machine state, never authored work.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
.playwright-mcp
.idea
.vscode
.synthesis

